    "summary": "High‑energy San Diego show with blazing Bertha and soaring Space>Other One",
    "blurb": "The February ’82 Golden Hall concert delivers a punchy first set highlighted by Bertha, Dire Wolf and a scorching Little Red Rooster solo. The second set climbs to a peak after Drums with an expansive Space → The Other One that showcases Phil’s thunderous bass and tight drum interplay. A crystal‑clear front‑of‑board tape captures the excitement for listeners who want the full experience.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Golden Hall is a quintessential early‑'80s Dead night where the band rides a high tide of energy from start to finish. Jerry’s slide work on Bertha and his incendiary Little Red Rooster solo set the tone, while Phil’s bass roars through the pre‑drums jam and becomes downright seismic during the Space → The Other One stretch. Bob locks in solid rhythm on Greatest Story Ever Told and adds vocal grit on El Paso, and the dual drummers keep a tight, propulsive groove that fuels the post‑drums explorations. Lost Sailor into Saint of Circumstance glides with crisp interplay, and the show closes with quirky fun on Man Smart, Woman Smarter and Johnny B. Goode. The front‑of‑board recording captures every nuance – from the bright guitar to the deep bass – making this a standout entry in the 1982 run.",
